 "intro_text": "Scholia (sing.: scholium or scholion, from Ancient Greek: σχόλιον, \"comment\", \"interpretation\") are grammatical, critical, or explanatory comments – original or copied from prior commentaries – which are inserted in the margin of the manuscript of ancient authors, as glosses. One who writes scholia is a scholiast. The earliest attested use of the word dates to the 1st century BC.",
